{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/814058-ever-borrowed-an-idea-from-a-novel-or-movie","id":814058,"title":"Ever Borrowed An idea from a novel or Movie?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-22T05:20:40-08:00","id":814058,"title":"Ever Borrowed An idea from a novel or Movie?","content":"Im thinking about The game i will run soon.<br /> Basically a town in The Middle of The desert being slowly overun by vampires (leaded by a Baali). Im going for The Salem's Lot kind of Story for HtR. In my game The vampires will be able to fly and wall crawl, among other things.<br /> <br /> But yeah, ever took sn existing idea for a game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:39:56-08:00","id":814318,"title":"","content":"Hundreds of times. sometimes the same idea from different perspectives or entirely new ones.<br /> <br /> Deserts, vampires, religious or occult themes...From Dusk till Dawn or John Carpenters Vampires come to mind. Both good fun for a Hunter game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T14:46:46-08:00","id":814462,"title":"","content":"I'm running a Vampire game set in Arkham, Massachusetts. It's heavily influenced by HP Lovecraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T19:19:01-08:00","id":814599,"title":"","content":"Doesn't even stop there, I regularly draw inspiration and ideas from random stories I've heard told throughout my life and even draw directly from memory and incorporate it in various forms or otherwise spin it into something I can use. Any idea that can lead to something fun is fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T22:52:54-08:00","id":814682,"title":"","content":"All the time. I just try my best to rub off the serial # so it is not obvious what I am stealing from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T08:48:38-08:00","id":814862,"title":"","content":"Are you kidding? of course we do! My last turn as storyteller i ran a Changeling: the Lost chronicle (my group plays both classic and new sorry &quot;Chronicles&quot;). We ran through four stories where I ripped the basic plots off and mashing together the following movies: Silence of the Lambs and the Princess Bride, Ocean's 11 and Labyrinth , China Town and Stardust and Good Fellas and The Lord of the Rings.<br /> <br /> The time before that I ran a Vampire: the Masquerade game that focused on a coming Sabbat siege and based the plots and characters off of Zero Dark Thirty, the Hurt Locker, The Re-animator and The Untouchables. Blend them all together and mix in a liberal amount of the various vampire lit and movies the clans are based on and you have a good Vampire the Masquerade game.<br /> <br /> The Time before that was a Mage the Ascension game based on a combination of Tron, Willow, 2001: A Space Odyssey and The Craft. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T22:57:43-08:00","id":816689,"title":"","content":"I am currently borrowing parts of Transcendence (not exactly a great movie, I know^^) for a W:TA game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7182-curiel","name":"Curiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:22:14-08:00","id":822483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/814058-ever-borrowed-an-idea-from-a-novel-or-movie#post814058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im thinking about The game i will run soon.<br /> Basically a town in The Middle of The desert being slowly overun by vampires (leaded by a Baali). Im going for The Salem's Lot kind of Story for HtR. In my game The vampires will be able to fly and wall crawl, among other things.<br /> <br /> But yeah, ever took sn existing idea for a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the time, the point of being a Storyteller is to be entertaining, not to be original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}